# Paw Connection — Project Context

## Repository layout
- `apps/api` — NestJS backend (Clean Architecture, DDD, Prisma, domain events)
- `apps/app` — Expo / React Native mobile app (Expo Router, tab pager)

## Where rules apply
| Area | Path | Primary rules |
|------|------|---------------|
| Backend | `apps/api/**` | 02-ddd, 04-api, 05-event-driven, 06-clean-architecture, 07-database, 08-security |
| Mobile | `apps/app/**` | 01-constitution, 03-testing, 08-security; follow existing component/hook patterns |
| Git / PR | whole repo | 09-git-flow |

## Rule precedence
1. **Project rules** in `.cursor/rules/` (this repo)
2. **User rules** in Cursor settings — unless they conflict with project git/commit standards; then **09-git-flow** wins for format and branching
3. Global `~/.cursor/rules` — superseded by project copies here for this workspace

## Before any change
1. Read applicable `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` for the files you will touch
2. Read surrounding code and match conventions
3. Keep diffs minimal and scoped to the request

## Commit scopes (Conventional Commits)
Use `api`, `app`, or module name: `chat`, `inbox`, `feed`, `auth`, `profile`, `media`, `infra`

## ADRs
Significant architectural decisions → add `docs/adr/NNNN-title.md` (see `docs/adr/README.md`)
